<id/19/1955/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Coral"@en ;
    skos:broadMatch <customs-1866/sea_life/#concept> ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_fertilizers_animal_materials/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "the natural skeleton or organ of support of a species of polypi of which some varieties are imported for ornaments. The chief coral fisheries are in the Mediterranean and Red Sea, and the Persian gulf. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 118]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated fields — definition use: Auto-match had picked Watt on coral reefs as a lime source; heading is ornamental coral."@en ;
